<Project>

  <!-- AC-1033: makes a `Docs` folder beside the project file into shipped documentation, without the author
       writing anything. Two jobs, and the second is the one that matters.

       It embeds what is there, so "adding a page is adding a file" is literally true — no Include to remember,
       nothing to keep in step with the folder.

       And it sets WithCulture="false", which is not a nicety. MSBuild's AssignCulture reads `welcome.nl.md` as
       a culture-specific resource and routes it into an `nl` satellite assembly, where the scanner never looks:
       the translation vanishes from a build that reports success. A plugin author outside this repository has
       no way to guess that, and would find out from a reader who could not see the page. Documenting it only
       helps whoever reads the documentation, so the SDK closes it instead — this file ships in the NuGet
       package under buildTransitive, and every project in this repository imports it through
       Directory.Build.targets.

       Remove before Include so declaring the same files by hand stays harmless rather than embedding them
       twice. Set CockpitHelpDocsEnabled=false to opt a project out entirely. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(CockpitHelpDocsEnabled)' != 'false' And Exists('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\Docs')">
    <EmbeddedResource Remove="Docs\**\*.md;Docs\**\*.png;Docs\**\*.jpg;Docs\**\*.jpeg;Docs\**\*.gif;Docs\**\*.webp;Docs\**\*.svg" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Docs\**\*.md;Docs\**\*.png;Docs\**\*.jpg;Docs\**\*.jpeg;Docs\**\*.gif;Docs\**\*.webp;Docs\**\*.svg"
                      WithCulture="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
